WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
If you encounter a large or deep wound where blood is flowing or spurting continuously

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
and does not stop with basic pressure, it is a much more serious situation.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.000
Major external bleeding.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:16.000
It's defined as severe bleeding from a large or deep wound

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.000
where blood is flowing or spurting continuously

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:22.000
and simply does not stop with basic pressure.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:25.000
This is a life-threatening emergency.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Your very first step is to call 911 immediately,

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
then have the person sit or lie down and apply direct, firm pressure using gauze or a clean cloth.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:40.000
If the gauze ever becomes saturated with blood, do not remove that bottom layer.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:44.000
Just keep adding more gauze on top and maintain that constant pressure.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:48.000
If your first aid kit has hemostatic dressings available, use them.

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:51.000
They contain a special chemical that helps blood clot much faster.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:54.000
After the bleeding stops, you can use a pressure bandage

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.000
to hold all that gauze in place while you wait for help.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:01.000
However, if the bleeding just won't stop and EMS has not arrived yet,

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.000
you may need to start packing the wound.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:08.000
This involves taking a stack of gauze, pressing it deep into the wound itself,

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.000
and applying direct pressure on top of that.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Let's practice wrapping a wound and holding pressure with a partner.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:18.000
I want you to place the gauze squares on one of your partner's limbs,

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:23.000
then use the gauze roll we passed out earlier to wrap around the gauze squares.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.000
Your instructor will demonstrate the wrapping technique first

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:30.000
and then you and your partner can practice together to make sure that wrap is secure

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:32.000
and applying steady pressure.

